x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+2{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+2{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2-8+6 \\\\ -1+10-9 \\\\ 7+2-9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false. Since statement ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+2{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true, we have ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ for ${x}_{1}=1,\\,{x}_{2}=2$ and ${x}_{3}=3.$\n\n- Statement “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent” is false. Since statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false, the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+2{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275386 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b450f31c-a7d3-5adb-b97f-c4019f0d24ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449768} {:answer/id #uuid "4962641e-6d35-5d45-8933-21ba34104b1a" :answer/type {:db/ide