r-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450840}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d5864d3-92dc-56c9-ae91-3d7c6bdd2052" :question/math-academy-id "q-157252" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $-6{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{3} & =-6\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12-8-4 \\\\ -6+4+2 \\\\ -12+7+5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false. Since statement $-6{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true, we have ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ for ${x}_{1}=6,\\,{x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=1.$\n\n- Statement “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent” is true. Since statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false, the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $-6{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$; “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275387 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f8fd2e6-05d0-5b30-963b-06e825131288" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449774} {:answer/id #uuid "39c69830-c567-5230-b180-445b08558fce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f8fd2e6-05d0-5b30-963b-06e825131288" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449774} :answer-field/id #uuid "679e9945-ad45-5f9f-bee3-cbf1a39c8865" :answer-field/key "$-{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450841} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65d6efaa-9a84-5e8e-b314-cdea60127cb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449776} {:answer/id #uuid "af932fb4-f3a2-5971-aec5-9759d804797b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af932fb4-f3a2-5971-aec5-9759d804797b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449777} :answer-field/id #uuid "841e39ca-c1bb-52f0-b7a2-17fd3182feb7" :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51338bd6-bb62-534d-8de6-e496d10b0226" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449778} {:answer/id #uuid "51453a9c-1b51-56c2-8aa2-856e4ff4a566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51453a9c-1b51-56c2-8aa2-856e4ff4a566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449779} :answer-field/id #uuid "a474f929-5eb8-5ab7-8b0e-320d9f1b2424" :answer-field/key "The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent." :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450843}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f4d0dbc3-088e-54a3-8420-9efcf1fc89b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-157253" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $-{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{2} & =-\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne \\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 4{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$\n\n- Statement “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent” is true. Since statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is true, the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$”; “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275388 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55ecca7e-205c-5e10-bf65-d3d1bbcd33f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449780} {:answer/id #uuid "35967e25-346a-5de9-bfb8-8a3dc6109d00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35967e25-346a-5de9-bfb8-8a3dc6109d00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449781} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fc873fa-b153-5bb8-a05a-68748c9b661d" :answer-field/key "$4{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field