ll that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $4{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2} & =4\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false. The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ {x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}=4{x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent” is false. Since statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false, the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $4{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363384 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9815692-a138-50b9-b4b5-53d1deb36416" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451341} {:answer/id #uuid "13928f2f-cd46-56fa-8c97-9a173d4