athbf{a}_{2}+x_{3}\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the solution $x_{1}=x_{2}=x_{3}=0$. A nontrivial solution proves **linear dependence**.\n\nTest the proposed combination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\mathbf{a}_{1}-2\\mathbf{a}_{2}-2\\mathbf{a}_{3}&=2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\ne\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe homogeneous vector equation gives the coordinate system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1}-x_{3} &=0 \\\\ x_{1}-x_{2} &=0 \\\\ -x_{1} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nRead a coordinate with just one remaining unknown at each step:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x_{1}&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_{1}=0 \\\\ (0)-x_{3}&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_{3}=0 \\\\ (0)-x_{2}&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvery coefficient must be zero. Thus the homogeneous equation has only the trivial solution and the set is **linearly independent**.\n\nA failed candidate alone does not prove independence; the homogeneous-equation argument settles the classification.\n\nThe statement “$2\\mathbf{a}_{1}-2\\mathbf{a}_{2}-2\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$.” is **false**. The statement “The set $\\{\\mathbf{a}_{1}, \\mathbf{a}_{2}, \\mathbf{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent.” is **false**. The statement “$x_{1}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+x_{2}\\mathbf{a}_{2}+x_{3}\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if $x_{1}=x_{2}=x_{3}=0$.” is **true**."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707089 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "522e8b37-f8de-5403-874d-f3bdac556699" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755997} {:answer/id #uuid "d4188e25-affe-5c55-acc6-79e13d0f8e1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answ